V8: "[enum cache] Fix enum cache leakage" (crbugs 575823799, a CSA_DCHECK
failure, and 579732799, not public; no CVE listed yet): for objects with
elements of which none is enumerable, the GetKeys* functions could return
an array from the enum cache that the caller didn't copy, leaking the
cache's array. V8 main commit 2d17e67d6b4cdf6095c418e5ac9531a86ed54d1d,
merged on 2026-11-02 to 15.7 (1dccf8995847d5c189b5c91d08b9cb8a40170dd0, for
157; not yet rolled into the 157 branch) and proposed for 15.6. This is the
15.7 merge, at v8/, without its test. Drop it once a 157 tag's V8 has it.

